<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ATHLETICS-SOUTH AFRICAN GRAND PRIX RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-SOUTH AFRICAN GRAND PRIX RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN, South Africa 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Tuesday's third and final meeting in the South African grand prix athletics series included:</p>
<p>Men:</p>
<p>100 metres</p>
<p>1. Frankie Fredericks (Namibia) 10.25 seconds</p>
<p>2. Brian Lewis (U.S.) 10.46</p>
<p>3. Ramon Clay (U.S.) 10.55.</p>
<p>200 metres</p>
<p>1. Patrick Stevens (Belgium) 20.54 seconds</p>
<p>2. Ramon Clay (U.S.) 20.68</p>
<p>3. Matt Shrivington (Australia) 21.10</p>
<p>400 metres</p>
<p>1. Iwan Thomas (Britain) 45.31 seconds</p>
<p>2. Arnaud Malherbe (South Africa) 46.14</p>
<p>3. Brad Jamieson (U.S.) 46.75</p>
<p>1500 metres</p>
<p>1. Abdallah Abdelhak (Morocco) 3 minutes 40.99 seconds</p>
<p>2. Hezekiel Sepeng (South Africa) 3:41.64</p>
<p>3. Ebeneza Felix (South Africa) 3:41.68</p>
<p>400 metres hurdles</p>
<p>1. Llewellyn Herbert (South Africa) 48.78 seconds</p>
<p>2. Ken Harnden (Zimbabwe) 49.18</p>
<p>3. Ferrins Pieterse (South Africa) 50.43</p>
<p>Javelin</p>
<p>1. Jan Zelezny (Czech Republic) 91.34 metres</p>
<p>2. Johan Vosloo (South Africa) 73.76</p>
<p>3. Johannes Van Eck (South Africa) 71.78</p>
<p>Women:</p>
<p>400 metres</p>
<p>1. Cathy Freeman (Australia) 50.96 seconds</p>
<p>2. Falliat Ogunkoya (Nigeria) 51.33</p>
<p>3. Adri de Jong (South Africa) 52.25</p>
<p>1500 metres</p>
<p>1. Kelly Holmes (Britain) 4 minutes 03.41 seconds</p>
<p>2. Gwen Griffiths (South Africa) 4:11.97</p>
<p>3. Alta Verster (South Africa) 4:12.48</p>
</text>
